{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789821714,"nonce":"PHj7BGGVlm8cPII5EaCs+Nx+a9M=","title":"haxe.xml.Parser.doParse is refused by every backend: the E0801 tag switch carries a SIMD8i32 arm","message":"`escapes.get(s)` in `haxe.xml.Parser.doParse` -- `escapes` is a static `Map\u003cString,String\u003e` -- reaches MIR with an unresolved receiver type, so it lowers to the E0801 runtime tag switch over every stdlib class with a one-argument `get`: IntMap, StringMap, ..., rayzor.SIMD16i8, SIMD32i8, SIMD4f, SIMD4i32, SIMD8i32. The SIMD8i32 arm unboxes the receiver into a register typed `Vector { I32, 8 }`, so `IrFunction::uses_wide_vectors()` is true for the whole function and Cranelift skips it (callers cascade to trap stubs); LLVM panics in VectorExtract (\"expected the VectorValue variant\"). Net: XML parsing never runs; Issue11883/4094/4096/TestXML crash at `Xml.parse`.\n\nTwo independent fixes, either suffices for this function:\n- the tag switch must not include SIMD (or any wide-vector) arms for a receiver that is not statically a vector -- a Map/Dynamic receiver can never hold one;\n- a static field's declared type `Map\u003cString,String\u003e` should resolve to haxe.ds.Map / IMap so the call is not \"unresolved\" in the first place.\n\n`RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1` now prints `[trap-stub:wide-vector] IrFunctionId(..) doParse` for the refusal; before this it was silent and only the callers' `[trap-stub:cascade]` lines showed.","files":null}]}